					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 16.0, 16.0, 836.0, 117.0 ],
					"text" : "Please note this patch assumes you are already familiar with the D4.calc~-example patch.\n\nThis is an example of how you can potentially use the D4.calc~ and supporting abstractions (highlighted in red below). This time around, we focus on the use of a custom D4.cell.mask2phasor~ abstraction that allows a phasor-based amplitude control based on the calculated mask.\n\nTo test, you will need to pair this with the D4.mask.editor.custom as the output in this case is tied to the mask which by default using D4.cell.mask2phasor~ output abstraction is 0. Turn on the ezdac~ and slowly bring up the main output level and explore changes in phasor rate per loudspeaker based on the mask."
				}

			}
